FG-DUCS research artifact
==========================

This release directory contains reviewed evidence, protocol material,
original analysis/checking code, and a source-rebuild overlay. It intentionally
does not contain the full MTSA source tree, an MTSA binary, packaged third-party
dependencies, historical backups, or private workspace metadata.

MTSA is a third-party project and is not relicensed by this artifact. Reviewers
must obtain the pinned upstream source from its official distribution and
verify the registered digest before applying the source-rebuild overlay. The
overlay's own README and manifest define the included and excluded boundary.

The current source overlay includes unfinished M9 compile-time plumbing, but
the reproduction workflows do not invoke it and no scientific claim counts it.
Two unused M9 constants that fingerprint private path-bearing control files are
zeroed in the public projection; the rebuilt proposal and its 95 scoped tests
therefore describe the public projection, not byte identity with a private tree.
The ARDrone, Travel Agency, and other source-anchored materials are described
as adaptations or provenance anchors, not as native FG-DUCS contracts unless
the accompanying evidence explicitly says so. No upstream bytes of the
unfinished M9 panel are included.

The MIT text applies only to material for which the FG-DUCS authors hold the
necessary rights. It does not relicense MTSA, upstream examples, or third-party
material. `RIGHTS_REVIEW.md` records the authors' confirmation of permission to
modify and publish the MTSA/DUCS-based tool, separately from unresolved
contributor/derived-input classes. Tool permission is not a blanket MIT
license for every file. No permission or endorsement is inferred from
citation, hashing, or the repository already being public. Omitted upstream
source, binaries, and dependencies remain omitted.
